WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.090
You're in a new city, you find a restaurant you'd love to try.

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.100
But the menu leaves you guessing.

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:07.680
What is this dish?

4
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:08.820
Will I enjoy it?

5
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.570
And what does it really cost?

6
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.920
That's why we built Dinevia, menus without borders.

7
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:19.560
Let's start with a simple Romanian menu.

8
00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:23.920
This is a fictional example processed by the real application.

9
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.960
A guest can paste a restaurant's menu link or upload a photograph.

10
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.280
No account is needed.

11
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.380
Choose a language and translate.

12
00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:37.120
Meta Muse Spark reads the photograph, identifies the menu text, and

13
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:40.260
translates the dishes and descriptions.

14
00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:45.580
Dinevia checks the response and keeps the original prices and portions.

15
00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.760
Here is the result in English.

16
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.320
Tomato salad, its ingredients, and its original price.

17
00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:54.420
Then chicken soup.

18
00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.990
A clear menu you can actually use at the table.

19
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.640
The original is still available.

20
00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:05.940
When the waiter comes over, you can show the exact dish you want.

21
00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.440
Now make it personal.

22
00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.340
Say you love tomatoes, but don't eat chicken.

23
00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.480
Open for you.

24
00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:17.390
The salad is a great match, while the soup conflicts with your preferences.

25
00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.960
The explanation tells you why, and both dishes keep their prices and

26
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:28.120
descriptions. These are taste suggestions, not allergy guarantees.

27
00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.220
Next, choose your currency.

28
00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:34.640
Dinevia shows an approximate conversion beside the original price,

29
00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.280
using published exchange rates.

30
00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.730
The model doesn't invent a price.

31
00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.320
Traveling with friends, switch the menu language.

32
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:46.870
The photograph only needs to be recognized once.

33
00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:51.320
Translations are cached for reuse, and the interface follows the selected

34
00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:55.800
language. Meta is central to this experience.

35
00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:00.860
Muse Spark handles visual recognition, translation, and preference

36
00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:06.000
reasoning. Our application adds source checks, numeric validation,

37
00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:09.370
private guest sessions, and caching.

38
00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:14.920
An experimental host workflow also uses Muse Image to explore preserving

39
00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.200
a restaurant's original menu design.

40
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.780
We started with an everyday problem in Moldovan restaurants and built

41
00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.680
for anyone eating somewhere new.

42
00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:30.880
Dinevia, local menu, your language,
your preferences, your currency.
